speechtext:
Madam Speaker, you will know that yesterday I tried to move a motion relating to the televising of the Special Joint Committee on the Constitution and was not given unanimous consent at that time. It is my understanding that I will have that consent now.
Therefore I would like to move the following motion:
That, notwithstanding the report of the Standing Committee on Elections, Privileges, Procedures and Private Members' Business concurred in by the House on October 20, 1989, the following will be the order of priority for access to the parliamentary channel during the mandate of the special joint committee on the Government of Canada's proposals for a renewed Canada.

October 10, 1991
Routine Proceedings
(1)	House of Commons proceedings live;
(2)	Replay of Statements under Standing Order 31 and of Question
Period;
(3)	Proceedings of the special joint committee live where that is
technically feasible;
(4)	Replay of proceedings of the special joint committee;
(5)	Replay of House proceedings or portion thereof beginning with
Question Period;
(6)	Weekend replay of the previous week's proceedings of the
special joint committee.
